 underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs and unresolved picker comparison prerequisite. Partial code supplies no additional scope authorization.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nAll programs, tests, font probes, and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- Exercise checkbox diagnostics across checked/unchecked, enabled/disabled, focused/unfocused, and collapsed/expanded states. Preserve strict full-label assertions and negative controls detecting widget or compositor text loss; verify bounded failures do not mutate or recollect evidence.\n- Run the failing advanced create-table scene first on Python 3.14/latest dependencies and the canonical coverage environment. Preserve diagnostics from the actual failing state, with exact source and dependency bindings.\n- Run SVG comparison tests covering lossless bytes/hashes, declaration-only font changes, limits, unavailable fonts, renderer failures, ordinary-PNG reuse, and explicit incomplete results.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, movement/history, caret, button-color, selector/completion, type-menu containment, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Obtain exact-candidate coverage JSON through the coordinator. Historical run `38897073714` missed branch and combined ratchets; use current missing lines/arcs to target meaningful task-related regressions. Do not weaken assertions or lower targets.\n- Preserve four picker comparisons—raw/framed with original/DejaVu declarations—through bounded geometry JSON. Verify decoded hashes and independently inspect all four images. System font matching does not establish the renderer-selected font.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review covering pinned dev, all changelog conflict resolutions, and the complete preserved task before coding.\n- Require exact-candidate static/lint/format/type checks, coverage ratchets, artifact checks, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate route for diagnosis and all 46 full-scene captures. Bind artifacts to candidate, checkpoint, task, and plan.\n- After checkbox and picker evidence identifies the first failing layer, produce concrete repair plans for independent review before production changes. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved.\n- Require independent implementation review and passing geometry checks plus individual full-PNG verdicts before publishing a correction. Revalidate against subsequent dev changes.\n- Preserve credentials, owner vetoes, provenance, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. Recommendation resolution does not replace those approvals.\n- The coordinator retains the RPi recommendation-policy/restart companion work, preserving genuine-input and security holds, and monitors PR #9 plus every task-related companion/repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a7fdaee407cb54717777ca2d6fc954e553bb44ab2e0ca1979ff9dc8db8d501d6","text":"# Correct PR #9 CI and preserve the complete SQL Explorer task\n\n## Summary\n\nCorrect the verified failures for head `49a16ba6f44cfa30e986aa62cec96ad0de9f47e0` in GitHub run `38915766002`, against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nThe resolver selected the complete-fixture approach. No further implementation choice is outstanding for this bounded correction. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint and evidence-first sequence; picker repair remains dependent on comparison evidence.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/selector_diagnostics.py`, mount a real `Collapsible` with ID `create-table-advanced` after the existing Select. Keep the selector’s default geometry and all completeness, full-row, label, arrow, and visibility assertions. Assert that the collected collapsed state matches the mounted panel. Retain the separate missing-panel negative control.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`, extract the per-region loop body into a private helper accepting the target, composed strips, result, and remaining row budget, and returning the updated budget. Preserve target order, entry insertion order, checkbox observations, invisible-region handling, row consumption, exception containment, limits, and missing/omission messages. Keep scene setup and final visibility checks in `terminal_diagnostics`; resolve PLR0912 without adding a suppression.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/checkbox_diagnostics.py` and `tests/agent_tools/svg_evidence.py`. Preserve every test, assertion, fixture byte, hash expectation, and diagnostic limit.\n- Fully read each edited file through its final page before writing. Preserve recovered source/documentation and existing changelog history; record the correction through the managed fragment mechanism.\n- Keep public APIs, diagnostic JSON shape, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 support, supported Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n\n## Feature and diagnostic requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, batch editing, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down cursor toggling.\n- Preserve document-order clipboard fragments for Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve paste precedence: matching fragments, then matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Keyboard, command, and terminal paste share the rules; changed clipboard text invalidates metadata and empty paste does nothing.\n- Preserve readable SQL and visible thin primary/secondary carets, using vertical bars where supported and underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs. Preserve checkbox failing-state diagnostics without recollection and the unresolved four-way picker comparisons: raw/framed SVG with original/DejaVu terminal-font declarations, exact hashes, lossless bounded geometry-JSON transport, and explicit incomplete results.\n- This correction changes no production checkbox or picker presentation. Select any further repair only after evidence establishes its cause and a concrete repair plan receives independent review.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run selector diagnostics in minimum and current Textual environments. Require the repaired fixture’s complete child rows and advanced context to pass, while missing, hidden, clipped, zero-height, and concealed-child controls still detect failures.\n- Run checkbox and render-diagnostic regressions covering checked/disabled/focused/advanced states, original-snapshot preservation, missing context, invisible regions, row/region/cell limits, and collection failures. Preserve exact diagnostic behavior through the helper extraction.\n- Run SVG-evidence and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/history, caret, button-color, selector/completion, and type-menu checks.\n- Require fresh exact-candidate lint/format/type checks, canonical coverage and ratchets, artifact smoke tests, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks. The current coverage job stopped at the fixture failure; it does not establish a new coverage shortfall. Obtain coverage JSON through the coordinator before selecting any additional coverage correction.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate route for all 46 scenes and four picker comparisons. Bind artifacts to the candidate, checkpoint, task, and plan; verify extracted hashes and independently inspect comparison images. Successful capture alone establishes neither a repair cause nor visual approval.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and independent implementation review for the resulting head and dev base. Revalidate if dev changes.\n- Require every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict to pass before correction publication. Unresolved picker evidence remains a blocker requiring further diagnosis.\n- Preserve complete authenticated task history, provenance, credentials, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. Resolver selection supplies no such approval.\n- The coordinator completes the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and safely restarts agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving genuine-input and security holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion PRs, and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This CI correction is an intermediate step toward that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"358507414a8d1e59404d2fdc5ecbc61d9c704ed103e2afa7cb3d520108a62050","text":"# Preserve PR #9 and collect decisive correction evidence\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2` against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nThe four inspected picker images locate heading degradation at the framing boundary: raw images retain the `c`; framed images obscure it with either font. Framing changes serialization and scale together, so neither is yet established as the cause. The original coverage JSON and pre-assert menu trace were not retained.\n\nImplement a bounded diagnostic checkpoint, then independently plan the demonstrated repairs. No additional owner preference is needed for this sequence.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Preserve the complete feature patch, recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, original approvals, and chronological questions and answers. Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/checkbox_diagnostics.py`, preserving every assertion, fixture value, and negative control.\n- Instrument `tests/sql/explorer/type_menu_viewport.py` with a test-support snapshot collected immediately before its existing initial visibility assertion and after scrolling. Capture focused-widget identity, field focus/mount state, `type_input` identity, matches/index/accepted type, menu visibility, scroll offsets, field/menu/viewport geometry, advanced-panel state, and dependency versions.\n- Read queued-message counts and pending layout/refresh flags only where observable; mark unavailable probes explicitly. Bound each snapshot to 8 KiB, reporting omissions. Attach the original snapshot to assertion failures without recollection, event draining, retries, refocusing, or changing assertion order.\n- Extend the SVG evidence helper and database-picker capture integration with three diagnostic controls: XML-reserialized raw SVG at native size; a target-size frame preserving the original SVG interior bytes; and the existing XML frame at native viewBox dimensions. Preserve the original four comparisons and ordinary production PNG.\n- Retain exact SVG inputs, lossless PNGs, dimensions, renderer settings, versions, hashes, and explicit failures through additive geometry JSON. Count all comparisons toward the existing separate 4 MiB SVG and decoded-PNG budgets. Do not change production framing, picker presentation, font selection, or dependencies.\n- In `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, add an `always()` artifact upload after the quality job’s existing command for generated `coverage.json`, using a unique run/head-bound artifact name. Preserve command exit status and existing check requirements; explicitly report when no JSON was generated. Keep protected capture/controller workflows unchanged.\n- Document the diagnostic route briefly and record the correction through the managed changelog fragment mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Compatibility and retained behavior\n\nPublic package APIs and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support remain unchanged. Diagnostic interfaces are additive.\n\nRetain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n\nRetain document-order copy/cut fragments, empty multicursor clipboard clearing, whole-buffer single-cursor copy, and paste precedence of matching fragments, matching lines, then whole-text repetition. Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal handling and clipboard invalidation.\n\nKeep readable SQL with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback. Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs and RPi recommendation-policy/restart objective.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Test snapshot completeness, unavailable probes, truncation, serialization, and preservation of focus, queues, scroll, and menu state. Preserve the visible-menu, offscreen-menu, unchanged-value, and no-query assertions.\n- Run the instrumented menu regression first on Python 3.13/3.14 and canonical Python 3.11, retaining actual failures and dependency bindings.\n- Test diagnostic SVG controls for preserved text, styles, clips, coordinates, fonts, exact bytes/hashes, dimensions, limits, and partial failures using fake renderers. Verify ordinary capture output remains unchanged.\n- Obtain fresh canonical coverage JSON through the artifact route. Keep the **98.03% branch floor** and all debt/coverage baselines. Select additional task-related regression cases only from the actual new missing arcs.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/history, caret, checkbox, selector/completion, and capture-lifecycle suites, followed by required lint, format, type, coverage, artifact, compatibility, SDK, and aggregate fast checks.\n\n## Review and completion\n\nObtain fresh independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward. Bind new diagnostics and captures to their actual candidate, source, dependencies, task, plan, and GitHub run.\n\nIndependently inspect the new picker controls and menu observations before specifying production repairs. Inconclusive results require renewed diagnosis; successful capture supplies no visual approval. After a concrete repair plan and implementation, recapture all 46 scenes and require every geometry check and individual full-PNG verdict before correction publication.\n\nPreserve credentials, provenance, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. Revalidate against subsequent dev changes.\n\nThe coordinator must complete and safely activate the RPi recommendation-policy/restart companion work, preserving genuine-input and security holds, and monitor PR #9 plus all task-related companion/repair PRs through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a294f7d30580917dcca0900f202cc27955c1445ac0c53df2dd3f1c5acb11fa10","text":"# Correct PR #9 rendering and CI while preserving the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `7756937e843fe7ffcc30ab0c0ba2a58bf7d7cee2`, against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nThe complete current-head check records and failed-job logs identify lint, menu-fixture, coverage, and picker-rendering blockers. Seven inspected picker controls isolate heading degradation to target-size rendering; serialization-only and native-size framing preserve it.\n\nThe independent resolver selected supersampled export and an explicitly visible starting viewport. These choices require fresh plan review and validation; they establish no implementation or visual approval.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, original approvals, and chronological questions and answers. Fully read every edited file through its final continuation before writing. Revalidate against incoming dev changes.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`, render every ordinary capture at **2560×1600**, then reduce once to **1280×800** using existing Pillow’s `Image.Resampling.LANCZOS`. Preserve the 208×47 terminal grid, framing, aspect ratio, fonts, SVG contents, and production UI.\n- Put the shared rasterization helper in the SVG-evidence module. Scale the unchanged framed SVG using an outer SVG viewport with `viewBox=\"0 0 1280 800\"` and dimensions 2560×1600. Validate intermediate and final dimensions; propagate rendering failures instead of silently reverting to the rejected path.\n- Preserve all seven existing diagnostic controls as direct-render comparisons. Render `framed_original` independently rather than reusing the newly processed ordinary PNG. Add a separately identified supersampled comparison that reuses the ordinary final PNG.\n- Extend additive geometry evidence to retain the exact supersampling SVG, renderer settings, intermediate dimensions/hash, final dimensions/hash, Pillow version, and reduction filter. Preserve raw/framed inputs and distinguish direct rendering from the processed output. Keep the existing separate 4 MiB SVG and decoded-PNG budgets, explicit incomplete results, hash verification, and atomic geometry publication.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/type_menu_viewport.py`, settle the expanded layout, focus the type field, scroll it into view without animation, and settle before entering the existing assertion sequence. Assert that the field is inside the viewport with room below it. Preserve menu visibility/placement, subsequent scroll-out hiding, retained focus, unchanged values, and no-query assertions. Keep production positioning unchanged.\n- Resolve PERF203 in the menu-diagnostics support module by extracting package-version lookup and exception handling into a helper. Preserve observation order, missing-version reporting, snapshot contents, and non-mutating behavior.\n- Correct the five E501 findings and formatting in checkbox diagnostics, and formatting in the SVG-evidence helper. Preserve fixture bytes, assertions, negative controls, diagnostic limits, and exception containment.\n- Document the capture pipeline briefly and record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Feature and compatibility requirements\n\n- Retain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without creating cursors, independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and document boundaries.\n- Retain independent positions, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste retain matching-fragment precedence, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve clipboard metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL and thin primary/secondary carets: supported vertical bars with occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs. Existing partial code grants no additional scope.\n- Keep public package APIs, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged. Renderer evidence changes remain additive.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub. Private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Add fast rasterization tests using a fake SVG renderer and small in-memory images: exact input preservation, doubled dimensions, one Lanczos reduction, final dimensions, failure propagation, accurate hashes/settings, and correct ordinary-PNG reuse. Retain comparison limits, omission/failure controls, and capture-readiness rejection tests.\n- Run the repaired menu regression first on Python 3.13/3.14 and canonical Python 3.11, plus minimum/current Textual environments. Preserve bounded failure snapshots without recollection or assertion retries.\n- Use the retained coverage report from run `38943147406` to add meaningful editor regressions for its actual missing branches: unmounted idle handling, rendering without a theme, and a search highlight wholly clipped horizontally. Assert safe lifecycle handling, restored theme state, unchanged text/cell widths, and correct visible highlighting.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement/history, caret, checkbox, selector/completion, menu-observation, and capture-lifecycle suites.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type checks, canonical coverage JSON and ratchets, artifact smoke tests, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks. Preserve the **98.03% branch floor** and existing combined floor.\n- Obtain an isolated GitHub candidate capture bound to source, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies, and run. Inspect the repaired picker and all comparison PNGs, then every one of the 46 full scenes. Require all geometry assertions and individual visual verdicts to pass before correction publication. Supersampling is accepted only if the actual heading is readable; otherwise retain the rejection and renew diagnosis.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward. Revalidate changed heads and dev bases; preserve complete provenance and authenticated history.\n- Preserve credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator completes and safely activates the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and restarts agents waiting solely on routine choices, preserving security and genuine-input holds.\n- Monitor SQL Explorer PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion PRs, and every task-related correction/repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. Completing this correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"6b729f400f170ad12628c5a3e1de801ef212a6789ad7f0b6f9f4509a882b0eeb","text":"# Correct PR #9 test dependencies and formatting\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `cfa19a96f14c57203dc328d8fe797018ba53cc0c` against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback and failed-job logs establish two blockers: missing Pillow during test collection and a Ruff formatting finding. The resolver selected the bounded test-dependency correction. No further implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, add quoted `\"Pillow>=10,<13\"` to both latest and minimum matrix installation commands.\n- In `tox.ini`, add the same requirement to latest/minimum test dependencies and explicitly to coverage dependencies, which override the shared list. Preserve SDK-only environments.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/supersampled_capture.py`. Preserve every assertion, fixture, failure case, hash expectation and diagnostic limit.\n- Retain unconditional test collection; do not introduce skips or optional-import fallbacks.\n- Preserve public APIs, runtime dependencies, package extras and Python 3.8–3.14 support. Let pip select a compatible Pillow release within the declared range; verify actual versions on GitHub. Keep runtime-only minimum constraints unchanged.\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered source/documentation, changelog history and authenticated task history. Record this correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order copy/cut fragments, empty multicursor clipboard clearing, whole-buffer single-cursor copy and paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal clipboard handling, metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled export, comparison evidence and strict diagnostics. This correction selects no additional presentation change and grants no visual approval.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- First run the existing supersampled-capture regressions in clean Python 3.8 minimum/latest and canonical Python 3.11 environments. Verify Pillow imports, exact dimensions/hashes, one Lanczos reduction, failure propagation and comparison-budget boundaries.\n- Require Ruff lint/format checks without baseline changes.\n- Run focused SVG-evidence/capture-lifecycle, multicursor, clipboard, movement/history, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox and selector regressions.\n- Require the complete Python 3.8–3.14 matrix, canonical coverage JSON, existing coverage ratchets—including the 98.03% branch floor—type checks, artifact smoke tests, SDK conformance and aggregate fast checks.\n- Collection failure supplies no new coverage result. Use the new exact-head report before planning any further coverage correction.\n- Obtain the required candidate-bound full visual review: inspect the picker and comparisons, then all 46 full PNGs; require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass. Successful capture alone is insufficient.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward; the current reviewer explicitly left remaining source and companion review unfinished.\n- Revalidate against incoming dev changes. Bind checks, captures and reviews to the actual candidate, base, checkpoint, task and plan.\n- Preserve provenance, credentials, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator retains responsibility for completing and safely activating the RPi recommendation-policy/restart work while preserving genuine-input and security holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This CI correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"5af1df680f9f476de3e392cfa42e3787eb049e270f376b23d4aa337ee5d5e613","text":"# Complete PR #9’s history correction and changelog reconciliation\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete feature checkpoint and reconcile it against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nThe saved source already contains the selected shared history lifecycle and focused regressions. The remaining confirmed source correction is the changelog conflict. Validate the existing lifecycle correction without replacing useful work.\n\nComplete check records show successful CI for published head `806f89ee273a598686fe80d7a26a382acee5a47a`; those results do not validate unpublished checkpoint changes. Independent source, companion, and full-scene review remain required. No material owner question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, remove conflict markers at lines 54, 62, and 64. Retain all seven SQL Explorer entries and dev’s replacement-authority entry under Unreleased. Preserve every historical release section and version marker. Check the complete file for additional conflict markers.\n- Preserve `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`’s shared `_record_cursor_edit` and `_prune_cursor_history` implementation. Both cursor editing and indentation must record snapshots through that lifecycle.\n- Retain snapshots only for exact edit objects present in live undo/redo stacks. Preserve active and secondary selections, selection direction, and independent preferred columns for those edits.\n- Preserve pruning after undo/redo, idle maintenance for inherited edits, and no-op transactions. No-op edits must neither create duplicate snapshots nor destroy live redo metadata. Document resets must immediately release obsolete snapshots, including during widget construction.\n- Preserve `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py` and the existing concise task changelog fragment. Make additional lifecycle changes only if source review or GitHub regression results identify a concrete defect.\n- Keep public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors; preserve preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste distributes matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeats the whole text. Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal handling, metadata invalidation, and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL and thin primary/secondary carets: vertical bars where supported, underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture pipeline, recovered source/documentation, diagnostic evidence, and authenticated task history. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering. All execution occurs on GitHub.\n\n- Run cursor-history regressions first: repeated indent/undo/replacement, abandoned redo branches replaced by indentation, unindentation or editing, checkpoint eviction, document reset, explicit history clearing, inherited edits, and no-op preservation.\n- Assert observable text and cursor restoration alongside bounded metadata retention. Retain reversed selections and independent preferred-column checks.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Preserve branch **98.03%**, combined **98.92%**, statement **99.22%**, and all subsystem floors.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route for all 46 scenes. Bind capture evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies, and base. Independently inspect every full PNG and geometry result before correction publication; retain comparison evidence and explicit incomplete results.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review, then complete independent implementation review covering every diff continuation, diagnostic helper/test, capture/scene change, and companion implementation. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must complete and safely activate the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Record questions with resolver decisions; recommendations do not substitute for protected approval.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. Completing this bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ee81771267af8eec15d44668ff4aa88017da5dbfadea162fa68e370175ffd805","text":"# Correct PR #9 document resets and CI fixtures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `b346d04a90b5edc073a4c384eae98e3150b883f0`, against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies stale secondary cursors after document replacement and two test-fixture failures. The independent resolver selected **Reset state**. No material question remains; this selection supplies no implementation, visual, merge, or protected-policy approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, extend `load_text()` to clear secondary selections, old preferred-column mappings, and cursor-history snapshots **before** calling Textual’s implementation. Preserve Textual’s primary-cursor reset behavior and the existing method signature. Use only state initialized before `super().__init__()`; avoid mount-dependent selection helpers during construction.\n- Preserve shared history recording/pruning for edits and indentation, exact live-edit identity tracking, undo/redo restoration, inherited-edit maintenance, and no-op redo preservation. Keep idle pruning active.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, construct the eviction-test history with all required arguments: `max_checkpoints=2`, `checkpoint_timer=60.0`, and `checkpoint_max_characters=1000`. Retain explicit transaction checkpoints and every eviction, metadata-bound, text, selection, and preferred-column assertion.\n- Extend its parameterized reset regression for both `load_text()` and the `text` setter. Create mounted cursors and reversed selections across several rows with distinct preferred columns, populate undo and redo, then replace with shorter single-line text and empty text.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/completion_readiness.py`, complete the idle fixture with empty undo/redo stacks, cursor-history metadata, and a callback invoking the real pruning method. Retain assertions that idle reopens retained suggestions and leaves dismissed suggestions closed.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support, protected workflows, and diagnostic interfaces remain unchanged.\n\n## Required behavior retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection preserves independent preferred columns through reversal, short lines, and boundaries without creating cursors.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing supports multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste use matching fragments, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, vertical bars where supported and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. The inspected published-head picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Run the two failing modules first on canonical Python 3.11, Python 3.8 minimum dependencies, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest dependencies.\n- Reset regressions must assert one valid primary cursor, no secondary cursors or obsolete preferences, cleared history/snapshots, safe rendering after layout settles, and typing at only the reset cursor. Undo/redo must not resurrect the old document or cursors. Retain construction and unmounted-reset coverage.\n- Run existing history lifecycle, multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head static/lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Obtain canonical coverage JSON; retain **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed coverage test run establishes no new ratchet shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate on GitHub and independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication. Bind evidence to the actual source, candidate, checkpoint, base, task, plan, and dependencies; published-head captures do not validate new edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete implementation review afterward, including every diff continuation and the RPi companion implementation. Earlier incomplete reviews supply no approval.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of recommendation-policy companion work and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices, retaining question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not replace that overall completion requirement.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a07d171e6d4a09c77a547e9facb213584f0e78ae82abcdb5c2ab3d0a7c6c4974","text":"# Correct PR #9’s unmounted-reset test context\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `a30ce3df206677c416b34e06b99e97e80764d1f1` against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies four failures in the unmounted-reset regression. Python 3.8/3.9 lack an event loop; Python 3.10–3.12 lack an active Textual app. The independent resolver selected **Active app context**. No material question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, wrap the existing parameterized unmounted-reset test body in an asynchronous exercise invoked through `asyncio.run()`. Construct `SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession())` and enter `app.run_test()` before constructing either detached editor.\n- Keep both editors outside the mounted widget tree. Explicitly assert that each remains unmounted after construction and relevant operations.\n- Preserve all four parameter combinations, construction checks, no-op undo/redo checks, reset assertions, cursor/preferences cleanup, and empty history/snapshot assertions.\n- Retain the mounted reset/render/type regressions and shared history lifecycle unchanged. Do not catch or suppress Textual lifecycle errors, skip environments, or weaken assertions.\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered source/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Fully read edited files before writing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n- Public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic interfaces, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste: matching fragments first, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending second, otherwise whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled captures, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Inspected published-head PNGs supply no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run all four corrected cases and the complete cursor-history module on GitHub: Python 3.8 minimum/latest, canonical Python 3.11, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest. Require explicit unmounted-state assertions to pass.\n- Run adjacent lifecycle and completion-readiness tests, then focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/selection, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle coverage.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Obtain fresh canonical coverage JSON. Preserve **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate through the trusted GitHub route. Independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication, retaining picker comparisons. Bind evidence to actual source, candidate, checkpoint, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward. Review every diff continuation, including previously unfinished diagnostic/capture modules, associated tests, and immutable companion implementation and exact-commit CI evidence. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of the RPi recommendation-policy work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This test correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ba4a97a05feaf4f5a7f593f4efe5950150cbccf14aaf2b22dc7852d6d7a7bc9f","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer whitespace and reconcile PR #9\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `5b3b02d1a9c2afa93b6d0d4a1eac7dbfc03b828b`, preserving the complete feature checkpoint and authenticated history.\n\nThe rejected capture’s widget and compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: caret rendering replaces the separator space. The saved source already contains the selected whitespace-preserving correction and focused regressions. Preserve that work; the confirmed remaining edit is removal of three changelog conflict markers. No material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Preserve `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`’s correction: underline every in-document character, including spaces and all visible expanded-tab cells, for primary and secondary carets. Render vertical bars only in end-of-line or empty-line padding.\n- Preserve underlying SQL, whitespace, foreground/background colors, cell widths, selections, scrolling, ruler alignment and completion behavior. Retain wrapped and horizontally clipped tab handling.\n- Preserve the existing completion scene’s `SELECT c.c FROM` text. Completion must retain its suffix and produce `SELECT c.customer_id FROM…`; the evidence does not justify changing insertion semantics or adding another separator.\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, remove conflict markers at lines 73, 77 and 88. Retain all three feature-side entries and all ten dev-side entries under Unreleased, preserving historical releases. Check the complete file for additional markers.\n- Preserve the existing concise task fragment and updated caret documentation. Fully read files before editing; retain recovered tests and documentation.\n- Keep public APIs, runtime/test dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 and supported Textual compatibility unchanged. Preserve supersampling, diagnostics, selected narrow UI repairs, coverage targets and debt baselines.\n\n## Required feature behavior\n\n- Retain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Retain document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Retain shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering. Perform all validation on GitHub.\n\n- Run the existing caret-rendering and completion-spacing regressions first. Require primary/secondary spaces and tabs to retain text, colors and widths in widget and compositor output, with editor and command focus, wrapping and horizontal clipping.\n- Require completion opening to preserve the rendered separator; acceptance must preserve the suffix, cursor position and undo/redo behavior without executing a query. Retain occupied-text underline and end-of-line bar coverage.\n- Run adjacent caret-color, ruler, highlight, multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, completion-readiness, menu, checkbox/selector and capture regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint, format, type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined** and **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated capture of the corrected candidate. Independently inspect `completion-columns` and every one of the **46 full PNGs**, requiring all geometry assertions and individual visual verdicts to pass before correction publication. Retain picker comparison evidence.\n- Bind validation to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependency versions and dev base. Published-head successes do not validate saved edits.\n\n## Review, dependencies and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding. Revalidate coordinator dependencies and preserve the durable correction barrier; archived recovery receipts grant no current approval or dependent-PR release.\n- Require complete independent implementation review of every diff continuation, including diagnostic/capture modules, tests and companion implementation evidence. Earlier partial reviews remain incomplete.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve complete provenance, original questions/answers and planning records, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify the RPi recommendation-policy companion work, independent resolution records, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve security and genuine-input holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. Completing this correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"65168e2a36952fea016fd3db3f756554f4bdd454fbf2f12bb23b38f4e2c60478","text":"# Correct primary-caret colors and reconcile PR #9 with dev\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete feature checkpoint and reconcile against pinned dev `1f7ff62aeba3c27a307a606b80459bca78b2dfd5`.\n\nPublished head `b416cd92b239290298c3e51758fb4c5db143c29a` fails three focused whitespace-caret cases across all eight matrix environments. Its hash-bound completion PNG and widget/compositor diagnostics confirm native block colors beneath the underline. Quality checks also identify formatting in the caret-rendering tests.\n\nThe independent resolver selected **Native styling**. No material implementation question remains; that selection grants no plan, implementation, visual, protected-policy, or merge approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, replace pre-resolution cursor suppression with a private render-only theme adapter. Delegate Textual CSS resolution to a copied theme, then neutralize its cursor style before native rendering consumes it. Preserve all other resolved styles and restore the original theme in `finally`, including rendering failures. Keep the absent-theme path intact.\n- Preserve the existing underline overlay for every in-document character, space, and visible expanded-tab cell. Keep vertical bars exclusively in end-of-line and empty-line padding. Preserve text, foreground/background colors, widths, selection/search styling, scrolling, ruler mapping, and completion behavior.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`, retain every existing assertion and apply canonical Ruff formatting. Extend mounted coverage using the actual `TextArea.render_line`, checking syntax-colored text and the `SELECT c.c FROM` separator alongside existing space/tab cases.\n- Reconcile stale automation changes with pinned dev: restore `.github/agent/review_control.py`, `tests/repository/notification_metadata.py`, and `tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py` exactly to the pinned base. Their current differences remove newer notification and provenance safeguards.\n- Reconcile operations documentation using pinned dev’s current contract and source associations. Preserve useful feature-specific activation requirements without reinstating obsolete “staged, not active” claims.\n- Reconcile the changelog using pinned dev’s history plus every distinct feature entry. Remove only conflict markers and exact duplicates; retain historical releases and record this correction through the managed fragment mechanism.\n- Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered source, documentation, diagnostics, authenticated history, and useful checkpoint changes.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, diagnostic interfaces, coverage targets, and debt baselines remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors. Preserve independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, bounded snapshot retention, and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeat the complete text. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, supersampling, bounded comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Preserve completion suffixes and existing SQL separators. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run caret-rendering, caret-color, render-lifecycle, and completion-spacing regressions on GitHub with minimum/current supported Textual dependencies.\n- Require real widget and compositor output to preserve primary/secondary caret text, colors, and widths under editor and command focus. Cover spaces, expanded tabs, wrapping, horizontal clipping, syntax text, selections, search highlights, and padding bars.\n- Verify original theme identity and state after repeated renders, focus changes, missing styles, absent themes, and native-render exceptions. Preserve existing mocked unit tests alongside real-renderer coverage.\n- Run restored notification/provenance regressions and adjacent multicursor, clipboard, movement/history/reset, ruler, completion, menu, checkbox/selector, and capture suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors. The failed coverage test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated GitHub capture of the corrected candidate. Inspect `completion-columns`, then all **46 full PNGs**, requiring every geometry assertion and individual visual verdict to pass before correction publication. Retain picker comparisons.\n- Bind validation to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, task, plan, dependency versions, and dev base. Published-head evidence does not validate saved edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward, covering every diff continuation and companion implementation evidence.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve durable dependency/correction barriers, complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion, safe activation, recorded independent resolutions, and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Historical receipts do not release current holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"65b765782ecd88e9b234d2c3e237161bb1fbe780dae4e4d6874b6733b527774c","text":"# Correct PR #9’s remaining formatting failure\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `f0f0abc4346f085df2e9058b9613532b04f2c227` against pinned dev `1f7ff62aeba3c27a307a606b80459bca78b2dfd5`.\n\nComplete feedback and failed-job logs identify one blocker: Ruff formatting in `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`. Matrix, SDK, type, coverage, and artifact validation passed. The latest exact-head review reports complete source, companion, and 46-scene review without concrete blockers.\n\nNo material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Apply canonical Ruff 0.15.22 formatting only to `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`, using the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character line length, and LF configuration. Private coding workers make source-only edits; formatting verification runs on GitHub.\n- Preserve every test, parameter combination, fixture value, assertion, and negative control. In particular, retain real native-renderer and compositor checks for syntax colors, whitespace, primary/secondary carets, and original theme restoration.\n- Preserve the complete feature checkpoint and authenticated history. Do not reopen resolved production caret, completion, picker, menu, or controller corrections without new evidence.\n- Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism, preserving historical entries and package/README versions.\n- Keep public APIs, method signatures, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, diagnostic schemas, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n- Fully read edited files before writing and revalidate against any changed head or dev base.\n\n## Required feature behavior retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention, reset cleanup, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin underlines over every in-document character and expanded-tab cell, with original colors and widths. Reserve vertical bars for line-end/empty-line padding.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture, recovered documentation/tests, and bounded diagnostic evidence.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First verify canonical formatting and lint for the affected module. Require zero new findings without changing baselines.\n- Run its existing regressions alongside caret-color, render-lifecycle, and completion-spacing coverage on minimum/current supported dependencies. No additional tests are needed for formatting alone.\n- Require fresh exact-head quality, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, artifact, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branches**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statements**, plus subsystem floors. Current passing coverage supplies no reason for additional coverage corrections.\n- Obtain the required candidate-bound GitHub visual capture and independent review of all **46 full PNGs** and geometry results. Retain picker comparisons; prior-head evidence cannot certify the corrected head.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward, confirming the correction preserves assertions and the complete feature.\n- Bind checks, captures, and reviews to the actual source, checkpoint, candidate, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n- Preserve provenance, durable correction/dependency barriers, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion and safe activation, recorded independent resolutions, and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9 and all task-related companion/correction PRs through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete the broader monitoring objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"dd261ae545b847735e796b558078dd265282511e0f553ceb3fc6c330bfe6bc1a","text":"# Reconcile PR #9 with current dev and complete review\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete SQL Explorer feature while reconciling with pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`.\n\nPublished head `ae84e66f77366547be44580cbdd5d5c9f51140bd` has 12 passing non-review checks and a final receipt recording 46 scene passes against the previous base. Independent whole-feature review remains incomplete. Those results do not validate the forthcoming reconciliation.\n\nThe recorded answer selects **Preserve dev safeguards**. No material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Restore these files byte-for-byte from immutable pinned dev:\n  - `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`\n  - `.github/workflows/agent-visual.yml`\n  - `tests/repository/capture_artifact.py`\n  - `agent_tools/task_evidence/1253260b20f14ee680edd15d01547757/parent-objective.json`\n- In `docs/GITHUB_AGENT_OPERATIONS.md`, retain all pinned-dev content, including failed-capture export limits and authority boundaries, plus the feature-specific recommendation-policy activation section.\n- Reconcile `docs/CHANGELOG.md` using pinned dev’s history and every distinct feature entry. Restore the five removed dev entries; remove only conflict markers and exact duplicates. Preserve historical releases and package/README versions.\n- Fully read each affected file through its final continuation before editing. Preserve recovered tests, diagnostic helpers, documentation, authenticated history and existing useful checkpoint changes.\n- Make no speculative editor, clipboard, UI or rendering corrections. Any newly demonstrated defect requires a concrete finding, focused regression and renewed independently reviewed correction plan.\n\n## Feature and compatibility requirements\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Preserve document-order fragments for Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin underlines over every in-document character and expanded-tab cell, retaining text, colors and widths. Reserve vertical bars for line-end and empty-line padding.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, completion suffixes, supersampling and bounded diagnostic comparisons.\n- Public APIs, method signatures, dependency declarations, diagnostic interfaces and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Focused coverage and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Verify restored files match pinned-dev hashes and that documentation/changelog retain both dev and feature content.\n- Run restored capture-exporter regressions first on GitHub, retaining unsafe-path, changed-file, capacity, partial-evidence and failed-capture controls. Reuse existing tests; add tests only for a demonstrated uncovered failure.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret, completion-spacing, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector and capture-diagnostics regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head quality, type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and existing floors: **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem and debt baselines.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated GitHub capture of the reconciled candidate at 208×47 cells and 1280×800 pixels. Require every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict for all **46 scenes**; retain picker comparisons.\n- Bind all evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies and current dev base. Earlier capture-stage pending fields do not invalidate the predecessor’s final receipt, but that receipt cannot certify new content.\n\n## Independent review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh current-base plan review before coding, followed by complete independent implementation review.\n- Assess every diff continuation, explicitly including `tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py`, `svg_evidence.py`, `visual_lifecycle.py`, associated helpers and capture integration. Track assessed ranges separately from retrieved pages.\n- Complete companion source/test assessment and verify exact-commit CI, installed-source identity, activation, rollback and waiting-agent recovery evidence. Preserve genuine-input and security holds.\n- Preserve review progress and evidence across retries. Incomplete assessment must remain a review-routing issue; it supplies no product defect or correction approval.\n- Preserve provenance, dependency barriers, credentials, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. The reconciliation choice grants none of these approvals.\n- After complete independent approval and required gates, use the trusted merge workflow. Continue coordinator monitoring of PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ab2679dc24629062eb4499ec69be0ecedf4768a71b27496b508cfb6baf84cd40","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and validate the saved diagnostic checkpoint\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`, preserving the complete feature and authenticated history.\n\nPublished head `98508973146e4137a88eaacff9a4cc13f8e84d9c` has passing non-review checks but a rejected visual review. The inspected PNG shows separate ruler and gutter labels; secondary-caret visibility remains unresolved. Its geometry lacks the diagnostics now present in the saved checkpoint.\n\nThe recorded **Preserve ruler** and **Diagnose first** choices settle the approach. No material question remains unanswered.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Remove only the extra blank line at EOF in `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, retaining one terminating newline and every test, fixture and assertion.\n- Preserve the saved caret diagnostics in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`: actual selections, primary identity, preferred columns, focus, keyboard mode, scrolling, viewport and terminal-cell mapping; exact widget/compositor text, colors and style flags. Keep expected fixture state separate from observations.\n- Preserve single-export integration in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`: retain exact raw, framed and supersampling SVG inputs, ordinary PNG hashes, renderer settings and processing metadata through atomic geometry JSON publication.\n- Retain existing bounds: nine regions/carets, 24 rows, 208 cells, 256 parsed SVG elements, 512 KiB reduced diagnostics and 4 MiB combined lossless SVG inputs. Missing probes, clipping, limits and failures must explicitly identify incomplete evidence.\n- Preserve the mounted tab/database-switch ruler regression and scene metadata distinguishing the active-column label from the first gutter/text row. Retain overlap, shifted-mapping and missing-label negative controls.\n- Preserve current-dev capture safeguards, recovered source/documentation, selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling and picker comparisons. Retain the managed changelog fragment without changing package versions.\n- Keep collection observational: no new refocusing, event draining, retries, timing changes, scene-state correction or production/export presentation changes.\n\nPublic APIs, signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic JSON additions remain additive.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Multiple cursors per row, selection merging, independent movement/editing, atomic undo/redo, bounded history and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary carets preserving SQL, whitespace, expanded tabs, colors, widths and mapping: underlines in every in-document cell; bars only in line-end or empty-line padding.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before source correction.\n- On GitHub, first check formatting and run the existing multicursor-diagnostics, ruler, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions. Verify collection preserves state and distinguishes missing evidence from observed absent caret marks.\n- Retain Unicode, combining-character, wide-cell, expanded-tab, clipping, unavailable-compositor, limit, single-export, atomic-publication and readiness/geometry rejection coverage.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret and completion regressions, followed by required quality, type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks.\n- Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branches**, **98.92% combined** and **99.22% statements**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate GitHub capture route. Bind evidence to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies and run; verify extracted SVG and PNG hashes.\n- Independently inspect the new caret layers and full PNG to identify the first failing layer. Recorded underline styles alone cannot establish visibility. Inconclusive observations remain unresolved; a demonstrated production/export repair requires renewed independent planning.\n- Submit the ruler evidence for independent reassessment while retaining the current rejection. Require all **46** geometry checks and individual full-PNG verdicts before correction publication.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Complete independent assessment of every feature diff continuation, diagnostic/capture module, associated test and companion implementation. Track assessed ranges separately from retrieved pages.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve complete provenance, dependency barriers, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion, recorded independent resolutions, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve frozen rollout sources and completed deployments.\n- Monitor PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ba2ca6de6e000df75238880cfd1237b0f8fb42b4d83747a5e9cacaf901396d87","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and validate the correction checkpoint\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`, preserving the complete feature, useful saved edits, recovered source/documentation, and authenticated task history.\n\nComplete assigned feedback binds failed CI and visual rejection to published head `43852778725dc1bb13b91b7a735cafaf9bacf5f6`. It does not validate unpublished checkpoint changes.\n\nThe recorded **Narrow gate repairs** and **Faithful diagnostics** choices settle this correction sequence. No material owner question remains. First validate the saved journal correction and faithful diagnostics; use fresh GitHub evidence before selecting remaining presentation, export, focus, or layout repairs.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Preserve the saved correction in `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/journal_screen.py`: empty failed reads show the warning alone; successful empty reads show “No matching journal entries.” Populated pages retain their count and any warning. Preserve stale-generation rejection, recovery, controls, and query behavior.\n- Preserve `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`’s cell-based cropping: retain combining suffixes with a completely retained base, including across differently styled spans; preserve original colors/styles and expanded-tab cells; represent partially clipped wide cells faithfully without mutating observations.\n- Retain saved fixes for test-variable shadowing, compound assertions, long lines, formatting, and scene-collector complexity. Preserve every assertion, negative control, fixture value, diagnostic ordering, and failure-containment behavior. Do not add suppressions or change debt baselines.\n- Preserve the added command-caret and new-file diagnostics, associated scene/capture integration, and ruler lifecycle snapshots. Record actual focus, selections, preferred columns, scroll, cell mapping, widget/compositor rows and styles, screen ancestry, resolved alignment, geometry, pending layout flags, queue sizes, row lengths, and dependency versions.\n- Keep observations bounded: nine regions/carets, 24 rows, 208 cells, 256 parsed SVG elements, 512 KiB reduced diagnostics, 8 KiB lifecycle snapshots, and existing lossless SVG/comparison budgets. Explicitly identify unavailable, clipped, omitted, or incomplete evidence.\n- Preserve single-export ownership, exact raw/framed/supersampling SVG inputs, PNG hashes, renderer settings, and atomic geometry publication through the existing artifact route. Do not refocus, drain queues, retry assertions, alter timing, or force scene state.\n- Retain the managed changelog fragment and current-dev capture/provenance safeguards. Fully read affected files through their final continuation before any subsequent edit.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies, diagnostic compatibility, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support remain unchanged. Diagnostic additions are additive.\n\n## Complete feature requirements retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling, atomic undo/redo, bounded history metadata, and reset cleanup.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary underlines over all in-document characters, spaces, and expanded-tab cells; bars only in line-end/empty-line padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selection/scroll/ruler mapping, and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, ruler presentation/reassessment, picker correction, supersampling, comparison evidence, and recovered tests/documentation. Partial implementation supplies no additional scope.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n1. Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding.\n2. On GitHub, first run diagnostic lint/format checks and the existing multicursor-diagnostics, scene-observations, ruler/visual-state, and journal-status regressions.\n3. Require Unicode, cross-span combining marks, wide-cell clipping, expanded tabs, style preservation, missing compositor, bounds, unavailable probes, non-mutation, journal failure/recovery, and stale-result controls to pass.\n4. Retain the strict ruler focus and widget/compositor equality assertions. Capture their original failing-state snapshots without recollection. Obtain exact-candidate GitHub observations before changing focus, widths, assertions, or lifecycle behavior.\n5. Capture command-caret, keyboard-multicursor, and new-file scenes with the saved diagnostics. Independently compare widget, compositor, SVG, and full PNG layers. Recorded underline flags alone do not establish visible carets. New-file alignment must be traced through actual resolved screen/dialog layout before selecting its repair.\n6. Run adjacent selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret, completion, menu, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, capture-lifecycle, and restored safeguard regressions.\n7. Require exact-head quality/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK, and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON, **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. Failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n\nBind all observations to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, GitHub run, and artifact hashes. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved. Any demonstrated remaining repair requires a concrete renewed plan and independent review.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Keep existing visual rejections in force. After reviewed repairs, obtain fresh independent complete-feature/source review and all **46** candidate-bound geometry checks and individual full **1280×800 PNG** verdicts at the **208×47** terminal grid. Historical captures cannot certify new edits.\n- Assess every diff continuation and companion implementation; track assessed coverage separately from retrieved pages. Revalidate changed heads and dev bases.\n- Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input/security holds, owner veto/cancel, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility, activation and rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator, idle exit, and coordinator-owned drain pause.\n- Use trusted publication and merge mechanisms only after required gates. Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and every qualifying repair PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a7052639e6cfc2694f714789db06ed529351f2900652de1bbba7dac4277eacb6","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and trace the remaining ruler failures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `c1976299ef64679a9e1335825800277a3c6e9f15` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nApply the selected **Trace lifecycle** sequence: correct confirmed lint/format findings, restore inherited dev safeguards, and collect bounded GitHub evidence before choosing a focus or row-width repair. No material implementation question remains for this diagnostic checkpoint.\n\nCurrent logs establish unexpected editor focus and, on Textual 0.89.1, 205 widget cells versus 206 compositor cells. They do not establish callback execution order or the first padding divergence.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`, refactor `_targets` to assign the selected target list and return once. Preserve lazy scene-specific queries, target order, requested row counts, filtering, exceptions and diagnostic output. Resolve `PLR0911` without suppressions.\n- Apply canonical repository Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`. Preserve every fixture, assertion, parameter and Unicode/style negative control.\n- Add test-support instrumentation around the existing ruler regression and visual scene. Record callback scheduling and execution order for tab activation, database switching and deferred focus restoration; include active tab, focused-widget identity and remembered-focus identity before and after each observed callback.\n- Invoke each wrapped callback exactly once with its original arguments, return value and exception behavior. Preserve its scheduler and execution position. Install instrumentation before scene configuration and restore wrappers during cleanup; change no production tab/workspace behavior.\n- Extend ruler observations with original strip cell/character lengths, requested crop width, resulting lengths, region/content widths, scrollbar/gutter state and exact trailing text/style spans. Observe the strips already collected for that snapshot; do not pad, trim, rerender or normalize them.\n- Bound the lifecycle trace to 64 events and 8 KiB. Report overflow, unavailable probes and collection failures explicitly. Preserve the first failing snapshot alongside its trace; diagnostics must not replace the original assertion failure.\n- Retain exact focus and widget/compositor equality assertions, geometry checks and negative controls. Add no refocusing, sleeps, queue draining, retries or scene-state changes.\n- Restore `.github/agent/review_control.py` and the deleted `tests/repository/coordinator_scope.py` byte-for-byte from pinned dev. Retain dev’s coordinator-scope documentation plus the feature-specific activation section. Restore the three removed dev changelog entries while preserving all distinct feature entries and historical releases.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered source/documentation and the useful checkpoint; record this correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive; existing fields and budgets retain their meaning.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and document-reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs; bars appear only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, journal failure reporting, faithful combining-mark/style cropping, supersampling and lossless capture evidence. Remaining command-caret, ruler and new-file findings stay unresolved until fresh evidence supports a reviewed correction.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub. Private workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Test trace ordering, bounded retention, unavailable probes, cleanup and faithful forwarding of callback results/exceptions. Verify instrumentation preserves focus, text, selections, preferences, scroll and callback execution counts.\n- Test strip observations with unequal widths, trailing spaces, styled padding, combining marks and wide cells. Require recorded original bytes/styles and lengths to survive unchanged.\n- Run the instrumented ruler regression first on canonical Python 3.11/Textual 0.73.0 and Python 3.14/Textual 0.89.1, then the supported matrix. Retain expected failures and their original snapshots; diagnostic success does not require making the regression pass.\n- Run restored coordinator-scope regressions, adjacent ruler/scene observations, multicursor diagnostics, journal-status and capture-lifecycle tests. Follow with focused selection/clipboard, history/reset, native caret, completion, menu, checkbox/selector and SVG/supersampling regressions.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines. Failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n- Use the existing trusted temporary-candidate route and artifact transport. Bind observations to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependency versions, run and hashes. Preserve single-export ownership and atomic evidence publication.\n\nAfter independently assessing the new lifecycle, strip, command-caret and dialog evidence, produce a separate concrete repair plan for each demonstrated remaining cause. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding, followed by independent implementation review. Revalidate changed heads or dev bases.\n- Keep visual rejections in force. Before correction publication, require complete feature/source review and all **46** geometry checks and individual full **1280×800 PNG** verdicts at **208×47** cells. Historical captures cannot certify new edits.\n- Preserve complete authenticated history, question/options/answer records, provenance, credentials, owner veto/cancel, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator retains companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility and activation/rollback verification. Preserve notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Honor actual current runtime holds; historical pause statements neither establish nor release one. Preserve frozen rollout sources and completed deployments.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"243f9516de3a3cfd3dd817a81b491c72c30fcfcfc68c2c426fdcdee3e8488b3e","text":"# Correct the SQL Explorer harness and preserve the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `f04d007c090bff62a19a6c2adb7f91bc242d3ecc` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nImplement the recorded **Correct harness layers** choice. Current GitHub evidence identifies deferred focus restoration overriding scene initialization, and a comparison between raw widget output and styled compositor output. Correct those harness boundaries and the confirmed lint findings. Preserve production tab restoration and ruler presentation.\n\nNo material implementation question remains. The selected strategy supplies no plan, source, visual, protected-policy, or merge approval.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- **Order scene initialization** in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_scene.py`. Keep `tab-database-change` unconfigured until initialization finishes. Activate the target workspace and switch its database once. Use a scene-only, one-shot continuation after the real deferred restoration callback and its queued focus application; then request command focus once. Mark initialization complete through a subsequent queued continuation after that focus application. Delegate production restoration unchanged and exactly once.\n- Make readiness observe the intended active workspace, database and command focus. Lost focus must invalidate readiness without refocusing. Preserve existing capture rejection and first-failure evidence. Add no sleeps, arbitrary queue draining, assertion retries or repeated corrective focus requests.\n- **Compare equivalent rendering layers.** Preserve existing `widget_row` and raw-strip observations with their original meaning. Add an explicitly named styled widget row from native `render_lines`, using the widget-local content-region clip and mapping it once to screen coordinates. Compare it strictly with the corresponding compositor crop.\n- Require equal complete text, cell lengths and resolved foreground/background/style flags for styled-widget versus compositor rows. Preserve raw-versus-`render_line` fidelity assertions, exact trailing whitespace, original segments and lengths. Do not manufacture padding, trim whitespace or change ruler output to satisfy equality.\n- Keep diagnostic additions compatible and bounded in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`. Preserve existing limits, unavailable/incomplete reporting, first-failure snapshots, single-export ownership and atomic publication.\n- **Correct confirmed quality findings:** format `agent_tools/sql_explorer_lifecycle_trace.py` and `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`; resolve their E501 findings without changing output or fixture bytes. Extract cohesive assertion groups from the ruler regression to resolve PLR0915, preserving every assertion and negative control.\n- Update the diagnostic documentation to distinguish raw, styled-widget and compositor layers and explain ordered initialization. Record a concise managed changelog fragment; preserve historical documentation and release entries. Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing.\n\nPublic package APIs, production method signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without spawning cursors, preserving independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve clipboard invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve visible thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selection/scroll/ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, journal status correction, supersampling, faithful Unicode/style diagnostics, recovered source/docs and current-dev safeguards. Command-caret, secondary-caret and new-file findings remain unresolved until actual candidate evidence supports independent acceptance or a separately reviewed repair.\n\n## Focused regressions and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- Extend the mounted ruler/visual-state regression to prove restoration, queued editor focus, one command-focus request and readiness occur in order. Verify collection preserves focus, text, selections, preferred columns and scroll.\n- Retain independent production tab-focus restoration coverage. Test that later focus loss rejects readiness without another focus request.\n- Test native styled-row/compositor equality across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1, including trailing padding, nonzero origins, gutters, borders and clipping. Preserve raw-strip fidelity, combining marks, wide cells and styles.\n- Retain overlap, shifted mapping, missing-label and missing-gutter controls; extend controls to detect lost trailing cells and incorrect styled-layer colors or flags.\n- First run affected diagnostic, ruler-trace and visual-state modules on canonical Python 3.11 and Python 3.13/3.14 environments, then the supported matrix. Run adjacent multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, caret, completion, journal, menu, checkbox/selector and capture regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines. Current failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n- Obtain trusted candidate captures and independently inspect the remaining caret/dialog layers and every one of the **46 full 1280×800 PNGs**, with all geometry checks at **208×47 cells**. Bind evidence to source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Historical captures cannot validate these edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent review of this complete plan before coding, followed by complete feature/source and visual review. Assess every diff continuation and companion implementation; distinguish retrieved pages from assessed coverage.\n- Keep existing visual rejections effective until fresh independent review resolves them. Contradictory or inconclusive evidence requires renewed planning, never a forced pass.\n- Preserve complete authenticated history, question/options/answer records, credentials, provenance, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility and activation/rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout bytes, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Historical pause records neither establish nor release a current hold.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, recommendation-policy companions and every qualifying correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This harness correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a302bef0fb4a29e56cbd7c361d9212f7e8251bf94a8111d0a2c74e4fa738eab0","text":"# Correct PR #9’s quality failures and preserve the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `813432a565124a7f569c38cb6556757ff58cad24` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nComplete current-head records identify two quality failures: import ordering and test formatting. Python matrix, SDK, type, coverage and artifact validation passed. Historical visual findings remain subject to fresh independent review; their older commit associations do not establish current acceptance.\n\nNo material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/styled_rows.py`, correct I001 by moving the `SqlExplorerApp` import into the repository first-party import group, after the `agent_tools` imports. Preserve imported symbols and test behavior.\n- Apply canonical Ruff **0.15.22** formatting to `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, following the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character line length and LF configuration. Private workers make source-only edits; verification executes on GitHub.\n- Preserve every test, parameter, assertion, negative control, Unicode fixture, style expectation and diagnostic bound. Add no suppressions, skips or baseline changes.\n- Retain the complete saved checkpoint, recovered source/documentation and chronological task records. Fully read affected files before editing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Preserve public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic schemas and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors, preserving independent preferred columns, reversal, clamping and boundaries.\n- Retain independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole